Moseley's law states \(\sqrt{
u} = a(Z - b)\), so the linear plot is the square root of the frequency against the atomic NUMBER. Statement I is false because it plots \(\sqrt{
u}\) against atomic MASS, and atomic mass is not a smooth linear function of \(Z\) — this was precisely Moseley's discovery. Statement II is false as well, because \(
u \propto (Z-b)^{2}\), so a plot of \(
u\) against \(Z\) is a parabola, not a straight line. Both statements are false, option (C).
